# Level0 - Integer Comparison Bypass

## Context

The program takes one argument and converts it to an integer with `atoi()`. It then compares the result to `423` (`0x1a7`). If equal, a new shell is spawned with elevated privileges.

---

## Assembly Analysis Line by Line

```asm
push   %ebp
mov    %esp,%ebp
```
Standard function prologue — saves the previous stack frame and sets up a new one.

```asm
and    $0xfffffff0,%esp
```
Aligns the stack to 16 bytes — required by the ABI for SSE instructions and libc calls.

```asm
sub    $0x20,%esp
```
Reserves 32 bytes on the stack for local variables.

```asm
mov    0xc(%ebp),%eax
```
Loads `argv` into `eax`. `ebp+0x8` = `argc`, `ebp+0xc` = `argv` — standard cdecl convention.

```asm
add    $0x4,%eax
```
Advances the pointer by 4 bytes — moves from `argv[0]` to `argv[1]`. Each pointer is 4 bytes in 32-bit.

```asm
mov    (%eax),%eax
```
Dereferences the pointer — `eax` now contains the actual string `argv[1]`.

```asm
mov    %eax,(%esp)
call   0x8049710 <atoi>
```
Pushes `argv[1]` as argument to `atoi()` by writing it at `esp`. `atoi` converts the string to an integer and returns it in `eax`.

```asm
cmp    $0x1a7,%eax
```
Compares `eax` (result of atoi) with `0x1a7` = **423** in decimal. `cmp` subtracts the two values and sets CPU flags — but does NOT store the result.

```asm
jne    0x8048f58 <main+152>
```
`jne` = **Jump if Not Equal** — reads the Zero Flag set by `cmp`. If `eax != 423` → jumps to the error branch. If `eax == 423` → continues to the shell.

```asm
movl   $0x80c5348,(%esp)
call   0x8050bf0 <strdup>
```
Duplicates the string at `0x80c5348` (the shell path) onto the heap.

```asm
call   0x8054680 <getegid>
mov    %eax,0x1c(%esp)
call   0x8054670 <geteuid>
mov    %eax,0x18(%esp)
```
Gets the effective group ID and effective user ID — needed to set privileges for the new shell.

```asm
mov    0x1c(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,0x8(%esp)
mov    0x1c(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,0x4(%esp)
mov    0x1c(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,(%esp)
call   0x8054700 <setresgid>
```
Calls `setresgid(egid, egid, egid)` — sets real, effective and saved group ID to the elevated GID.

```asm
mov    0x18(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,0x8(%esp)
mov    0x18(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,0x4(%esp)
mov    0x18(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,(%esp)
call   0x8054690 <setresuid>
```
Calls `setresuid(euid, euid, euid)` — sets real, effective and saved user ID to the elevated UID. This is what grants us elevated privileges.

```asm
lea    0x10(%esp),%eax
mov    %eax,0x4(%esp)
movl   $0x80c5348,(%esp)
call   0x8054640 <execv>
```
Calls `execv(path, argv)` to launch the shell :
```
esp+0x00 = path   = 0x80c5348  ← shell binary path
esp+0x04 = argv   = &esp+0x10  ← arguments array
```

```asm
mov    0x80ee170,%eax
...
call   0x804a230 <fwrite>
```
Error branch — prints `"No !"` to stderr if the comparison failed.

---

## Execution Flow

```
argv[1] → atoi() → eax
cmp eax, 0x1a7
  ↓ equal          ↓ not equal
setresgid()       fwrite("No !")
setresuid()       return 0
execv("/bin/sh")
→ shell !
```

---

## Final Payload

```bash
./level0 423
```

`423` = `0x1a7` → passes the comparison → shell spawned with elevated privileges.

---

## Result

```bash
./level0 423
$ whoami
level1    ← shell obtained with elevated privileges !
```